    ["SPUT history", "By the daily-file test, 44 issuance rows are below the previous day's NAV: 41 before 2026 including 20 Jun 2025 (so 40 excluding it) and 3 in Jan 2026. One of them, 20 Jun 2025 (11,600,000 units at 17.25 against a prior-day NAV of 18.33, 5.89%), is a timing effect: an underwritten deal priced against the 13 Jun NAV; not an ATM sale. It is a bought deal through Canaccord Genuity (supplement of 18 Jun 2025): priced on 13 Jun (p12), net to the Trust 17.0376 per unit, equal to the 13 Jun NAV (p2), closing 20 Jun (p2); the NAV had risen to 18.2570 by 17 Jun (p2). The other 43 rows are shortfalls of 0.007% to 0.73% (18 under 0.15%, 25 from 0.15% to 0.75%; deepest 10 and 12 Apr 2024). The daily NAV is rounded to the cent (five rows are within half a cent of the prior NAV), and the 216 days on which the NAV is unchanged may make the prior NAV stale", "43 issue prices sit slightly below the prior-day NAV; the reason is not in the documents", "Limitation: unexplained and stated as a limit. An earlier count of unexplained rows could not be reproduced from any stated rule and was withdrawn. Sprott is not expected to answer"],
